  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 149 PM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nMid-level disturbance has pretty much cleared the CWA, with cloud \ncover and showers exiting to the south and east. Plenty of sunshine \nacross the CWA this afternoon as temperatures rise through the upper \n80s and 90s. Still several more degrees to go before the end of the \nday, all the while dewpoints remain high for many areas. Quite a few \nlocations are already seeing heat indices from 105 to 110 early this \nafternoon. No plans to change headlines and will let things expire \nat 02Z this evening. Still appears there isn't a need to extend it \nat this time as temps/dewpoints on Monday are coming in a tad lower \nthan what we saw this weekend. This keeps forecast apparent T's \nbelow 100 across much of the CWA.\n\nAlso watching convection chances this afternoon. CAMs continue to \nshow limited potential over the CWA, but will be keeping an eye on \nany developing cumulus within the weak surface trough later this \nafternoon. If there is any initiation, it would be within this \ntrough as it eventually sets up over southeast SD. \n\nWill need to monitor smoke trends overnight as HRRR-smoke product \nshows increasing concentration of smoke aloft and at the surface \ntonight through the day Monday. Satellite imagery shows quite a bit \nof smoke aloft across western ND and MT, even some of this making it \nto the surface as witnessed by a handful of obs from 5-9SM. Followed \ntrends of increasing surface smoke concentration in the HRRR to add \npatchy smoke wording to portions of the CWA tonight through the day \nMonday.",
